Each check declares an `options` block with defaults + types. Engine validates user's cofferdam.toml against each check's schema at startup; bad config fails loudly, not at runtime.

API:
```ts
defineCheck({
  options: {
    tenantFields: { default: ["siteId", "merchantId"], type: "string[]" },
    excludedResources: { default: [], type: "string[]" },
  },
  run(file, ctx, opts) { /* opts is fully typed */ }
});
```

Map to TenantIsolation's Credo `param_defaults` + `Params.get/3`.

Acceptance:
- TS types for options inferred from schema (autocomplete in run())
- cofferdam.toml `[checks."X"] field = bad-type` produces a clear error before any file is analyzed
- Options can be overridden in cofferdam.toml; defaults work without any config

GitHub: https://github.com/TAJD/cofferdam/issues/15

A plugin enforcing a project-wide rule scoped to a layer (e.g. 'no Math.random() in any file in the lib layer') has to redeclare globs in `defineCheck.files.pathPattern` instead of asking 'is this file in layer X?'. Engine already computes the mapping for `Design.LayerViolation`; plugins can't see it.

Add to SDK's `SourceFile`:
```ts
interface SourceFile {
  readonly path: string;
  readonly text: string;
  readonly layer: string | null;   // from cofferdam.invariants.toml [layers]; null if unmapped
}
```

Bonus: `FileScope` could grow `layers?: readonly string[]` for declarative layer scoping — engine pre-filters before invoking `run()`.

Concrete case: `Refactor.HyroxRng` plugin currently uses `pathPattern: "lib/{hyrox*,geneticAlgorithm}.ts"` — goes stale if files move within `lib/`. With `file.layer` it could be `if (file.layer !== "lib") return;`.

cd-5tz exposed file.layer on SourceFile so plugin checks can do imperative layer scoping:

  if (file.layer !== "lib") return;

Bonus from that bead (deferred): a declarative pre-filter so the plugin host skips files outside the declared layers before invoking run().

Shape:

  defineCheck({
    files: { layers: ["lib", "app"] },
    ...
  });

Implementation: extend FileScope in packages/check-sdk/src/define-check.ts; extend fileMatchesScope in packages/check-sdk/src/plugin-host.ts to consult input.layer; engine pre-filters before runPlugin invocation. Reuses the layer field already in PluginRunInput from cd-5tz.

Out of scope when filed: nested layer matching, exclude-by-layer.
